Z||000000||Mattyman||11-17-2001||11:15 PM||||Well, today I went with my mom to drop her Toyota off to get it inspected at our local mechanic.  As I was there I noticed a silver Fiero coupe sitting between some other cars.  Its either an 87 or 88, the paint is bad on it and im not really sure if it runs or not, but it had decent five spoke rims.  Well on the way back to pick up my moms car, I got out and checked it and the mechanic Art that I have known for along time comes out to talk to my mom.  I look at him after looking at the car and he laughs and says if you want it you can have it.  He knows I love them.  I guess there is some legal stuff with the car some guy just left it there and isnt paying for the repair or whatever it had.  So Art has to go to court and just wants to get rid of it and he said I could have it.  Hopefully everything goes ok and I can get it.  Would be good to fix up, but if it costs too much im gonna use it for parts.  Im excited. ||||reg||7
Z||000001||FieroMaster88||11-18-2001||01:01 AM||||Sweet!  Free is ALWAYS good.  Would be nice for another Fiero to be saved!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Good luck.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jamessig.jpg">                   <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>Not your ordinary 88 coupe!||||reg||14
Z||000002||Nashco||11-18-2001||03:47 AM||||If it's an 88 coupe, I'd be very interested in getting what's left that you don't want, especially the rolling chassis.  If you are interested in offloading the whole car, PM me, maybe we can work something out.  Again, only if it's an 88.  Thanks!  Cool find <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnF||11-18-2001||08:15 AM||||I can tell you - there is no such thing as a free Fiero.<P>I have an '85GT sitting in my garage under resto that I was "given" by my mechanic.  I actually drove it home.  All it needs is a "new" engine, interior, headlamps, console electrical sysem, windshield, sail panels, etc, etc, etc!  About $3500 minimum should do it!  Great body, though!<P>Before you bring it home, make sure you really want it.||||reg||10
